  "details": "Collaborative Group Events:\n\nThere have been many times where I myself or others have had a collaborative event with another group and aside from organising what will happen, the same problem and question always arises;\n\n\"Which group will host the instance\"\n\nWhilst it made sense when groups were first made to not add a need for this, groups are now being used so much more for events and even just general hangouts.\n\nAdding a feature to create an event and allowing the group owner (or users with the correct permissions) to invite another group to collab with the event would solve this issue heavily.\n\nHow I see this working/looking:\n\nThe owner of the group (or users within the group with the correct permissions) may invite another group during event creation as a \"collaborator\" for that single event.\n\nThe owner of the collaborative group will receive a collaborator invite for that event (this will prevent people from adding random groups to events) and they may choose whether to accept or deny.\n\nUpon accepting, the event will display on both groups and will say in the event details both groups names rather than one or the other.\n\nOnce the event begins, the person who creates the world will link it to the event (as you normally would when creating a group instance) and the instance will display in both of the groups instead of just one hosting, and when clicking on the world, if no name has been chosen for the instance it will display both groups names (like how hosting a group instance with no name currently displays the single groups name)\n\nOverall, this really helps push for more community involvement with one another and solves the biggest issue groups currently have with events.\n\nSure there are ways to get around it, but out of want for quality of life and more efficient ways to organise collaborative events with other groups so that we can easily and enjoyably work together and be more involved!",
